WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:03.740
After a long day, trust me there's no reason
that you can't make dinner at home.

00:00:03.740 --> 00:00:04.880
That's why today I'm putting the challenge

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:08.780
out there to see, if Mia can do in just under 10 minutes.

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:11.500
Welcome, to Ramsay in 10.

00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:20.300
Hi, I'm chef Mia Castro, and chef Ramsay challenged me
today to make a pasta dish under 10 minutes.

00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:24.480
and I'm making an all-time college favourite ramen 
Cacio e Pepe

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:28.640
It's pasta with Cacio - cheese, pepe - pepper,

00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:33.200
And, I'm using ramen because it cooks within 2 - 3 minutes

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:35.200
And you probably have it in your pantry anyways already.

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:37.600
So, let's start the clock and lets get started.

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:40.460
This is some, fresh ramen.

00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:45.120
If you don't have fresh ramen, which you can find 
in the refrigerated section

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:48.120
at, like your organic grocery store.

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:53.080
You can just use, your traditional, Uhm, your traditional package ramen.

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:55.940
They both cook in under 10 minutes.

00:00:55.940 --> 00:00:59.160
The fresh one cooks in 2 - 3 because it's fresh.

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:02.280
And the one in the package cooks in about the same time

00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:05.800
So all these ingredients are staples in my kitchen,

00:01:05.860 --> 00:01:11.035
so it's really easy for me to make when I've came home from a busy day at work

00:01:11.035 --> 00:01:14.830
or when it's really cold outside 
and I want something hearty.

00:01:14.830 --> 00:01:18.415
In here, I have a preheated pan.

00:01:19.805 --> 00:01:23.795
Just a little too hot, so I'm gonna let it cool down

00:01:23.790 --> 00:01:30.390
and I'm gonna put some olive oil, some butter

00:01:35.095 --> 00:01:37.605
They have Gordon's fancy Peppermill here

00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:42.485
if you don't have this at home, they sell them at the grocery store

00:01:42.485 --> 00:01:46.305
the disposable kind, either one works the same,

00:01:46.300 --> 00:01:49.345
you're gonna get the same quality meal.

00:01:50.985 --> 00:01:54.585
And I like to do the pepper straight into the butter,

00:01:54.580 --> 00:01:59.495
Cuz it gets it really aromatic.

00:02:00.700 --> 00:02:05.130
This is another one of those dishes where you don't have to measure everything,

00:02:05.130 --> 00:02:07.445
you kind of want to do everything by tasting

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:10.450
so it depends on how spicy you like it,

00:02:10.450 --> 00:02:12.290
how much pepper you're gonna add.

00:02:12.290 --> 00:02:15.535
I'm putting all the directions below anyway 
just in case you need it,

00:02:15.530 --> 00:02:18.640
but it should be pretty easy for you to make.

00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:21.500
I'm just gonna test one of these noodles.

00:02:23.340 --> 00:02:24.300
Great.

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:27.320
So I'm gonna go straight into the pan with the noodles

00:02:32.180 --> 00:02:35.440
And it's actually good if you get some of that pasta water in there.

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:39.820
Because it will help you make a sauce with the starch

00:02:43.880 --> 00:02:45.500
Bring it onto the pan.

00:02:45.540 --> 00:02:47.540
Stir it around

00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:52.560
and I'm gonna add a little bit of that pasta water in here

00:02:53.610 --> 00:02:56.980
and what that does is it makes a really nice sauce

00:02:56.980 --> 00:02:58.980
When you combine it with the cheese

00:03:00.470 --> 00:03:03.825
This is fresh grated Pecorino, 
you can use Parmesan as well,

00:03:03.825 --> 00:03:07.374
but I prefer the sharpness of the Pecorino.

00:03:09.150 --> 00:03:11.212
Few handfuls.

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:15.420
Move it around.

00:03:16.410 --> 00:03:21.495
And you can see there how the sauce is starting 
to form.

00:03:23.015 --> 00:03:25.915
Pasta is one of my favorite things to eat,

00:03:25.910 --> 00:03:30.230
but I don't always have time or I don't always really want to cook

00:03:30.230 --> 00:03:35.105
so I like using ramen in place of pasta in a lot of dishes

00:03:35.105 --> 00:03:38.315
and I actually lived off of it in college

00:03:38.315 --> 00:03:40.900
and I would make all sorts of different things.

00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:45.900
Spaghetti, the Cacio e Pepe, carbonara, you can use it anything.

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:50.195
Go with a little bit more water.

00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:57.915
And the beauty of ramen noodles is that

00:03:57.920 --> 00:04:01.360
it cooks a lot faster than regular pasta

00:04:01.360 --> 00:04:06.220
and it's cheap. So you don't have to go 
to a restaurant to get this dish.

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:12.780
I'm gonna go ahead and taste it.

00:04:22.215 --> 00:04:24.650
A little bit more salt.

00:04:29.415 --> 00:04:34.545
So you need to be a little more careful when you're using the traditional packaged ramen

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:40.290
because they cook faster so you probably want to cook them a little less when they're in the water.

00:04:40.290 --> 00:04:42.910
and as soon as they get really nice and creamy

00:04:42.910 --> 00:04:46.015
and you get a really nice tight sauce like that.

00:04:46.015 --> 00:04:48.080
They're ready to serve.

00:04:48.080 --> 00:04:50.625
I have plenty of time to make this look great right now.

00:04:53.720 --> 00:04:59.569
So you want to get fancy you just give it that nice swirl on top with the tongs.

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:04.610
Give it a little height. Picture-perfect.

00:05:07.345 --> 00:05:12.325
and then just finish it off with a sprinkling of Pecorino

00:05:13.950 --> 00:05:16.920
and some fresh cracked pepper.

00:05:16.920 --> 00:05:19.829
This is a dish that you can make in 
well under 10 minutes

00:05:19.829 --> 00:05:23.650
So there's no excuse for you not to make this at home

00:05:23.650 --> 00:05:25.295
So, boom.

00:05:25.295 --> 00:05:27.348
Ramen Cacio e Pepe, Gordon.

00:05:27.340 --> 00:05:29.970
Under 10 minutes and under $10.

00:05:32.730 --> 00:05:34.905
Leave a comment below on what you think of this dish

00:05:34.900 --> 00:05:37.285
and don't forget to subscribe to 
Gordon's YouTube channel.

00:05:37.280 --> 00:05:38.690
See you next time.

00:05:39.535 --> 00:05:41.145
Oh my god when I was in ramen

00:05:41.145 --> 00:05:43.197
Sorry *laughs*

